inline_comments.body:
The decision whether the ReplaySSM rings live inside the mamba state page (Triton) or outside of it (FI) is now duplicated in 4 places - `get_state_shape` / `get_state_dtype` here and `get_mamba_state_shape_from_config` / `get_mamba_state_dtype_from_config` in `nemotron_h.py`.
On main all of these just called `append_replayssm_ring(...)`. Let's keep this mechanism, but rename it to `maybe_append_replayssm_ring` and make it a no-op for FI. Something like:

```python
@classmethod
def maybe_append_replayssm_ring(cls, base_dtypes, model_dtype, backend):
    if backend == MambaBackendEnum.FLASHINFER:
        # FI keeps its rings outside of the mamba state page
        return base_dtypes
    return (*base_dtypes, *cls.replayssm_ring_dtypes(model_dtype))
```
(and the same for the shapes, calling `replayssm_ring_shapes`)

This way the page layout is decided in a single place, and all the new logic for getting the mamba state shapes / dtypes here and in `nemotron_h.py` can be deleted - these 4 functions can stay as they are on main (other than passing `backend` to the dtype function). Also, `get_replayssm_state_shape` can then call `MambaStateShapeCalculator.replayssm_ring_shapes` directly, so `_get_replayssm_ring_shapes` isn't needed.
